        /// <term><b>Summary:</b></term>
        /// <summary>
        /// <para>Generates virtual try-on images by replacing the clothing on a model with specified garments based on AI algorithms. This service preserves the model\&quot;s original details, posture, and facial features while ensuring a realistic and well-fitted appearance. You only need to provide the URLs of the original product images to obtain the processed images.</para>
        /// </summary>
        /// 
        /// <term><b>Description:</b></term>
        /// <description>
        /// <h1>Product overview</h1>
        /// <para>Virtual try-on is an AI-based image generation API service that replaces the clothing on a model with specified garments based on user-provided clothing and model images. The service preserves the model\&quot;s other details and image details without changing the model\&quot;s posture or facial features, ensuring a realistic and well-fitted appearance. You only need to provide the URL of the original product image to obtain the processed image.</para>
        /// <h1>Scenarios</h1>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><b>Virtual try-on for clothing, shoes, and hats:</b></description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <para>Supports virtual try-on for 14 categories of clothing, shoes, and hats, including tops, coats, bottoms, dresses, jumpsuits, socks, shoes, hats, earrings, necklaces, bracelets, scarves, bags, and glasses. After you upload a person image and a product image, the system intelligently matches the product position and proportion based on the person\&quot;s posture and body parts. This generates natural and realistic try-on effects, intuitively displaying the on-body performance of the clothing and presenting a coordinated and realistic wearing effect.</para>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><para><b>Model replacement (model skin or face replacement)</b></para>
        /// <para>You provide the original model scene image and the face or reference image of the target model to apply the target person\&quot;s face to the original model. This is suitable for customer-specified models, unified brand images, and character image adaptation for different markets. It also reduces the duplication of using the same model image as other merchants.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Posture replacement (posture fission)</b></para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <para>You provide the original model scene image and a posture reference image with a specified pose to generate the effect of the original person and outfit in the new posture. This displays the fit, silhouette, and on-body performance of the product in different postures such as standing, raising hands, and turning around.</para>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><b>E-commerce product display and marketing:</b></description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <para>Helps merchants quickly generate model try-on images for different products, reducing the costs of traditional shooting, outfit changes, and post-production, and improving the production efficiency of product images.</para>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><b>Online shopping experience optimization:</b></description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <para>Consumers can preview the wearing effect of products through virtual try-on, more intuitively understand the style, matching, and overall effect of the products, assist in purchase decisions, and enhance the shopping experience.</para>
