        /// <term><b>Summary:</b></term>
        /// <summary>
        /// <para>Generates multiple versions of e-commerce videos by replacing products or characters in a template video. This AI video service covers video understanding, element replacement, quality verification, and result delivery. It focuses on product and character consistency, detail restoration, conversion expression, and large-scale production. By retaining the original actions, camera rhythms, and marketing structures, it rapidly generates multi-version content to reduce shooting, editing, and adaptation costs.</para>
        /// </summary>
        /// 
        /// <term><b>Description:</b></term>
        /// <description>
        /// <h2><b>Product introduction</b></h2>
        /// <para>E-commerce video variation generation is an AI video service for product content production, covering video understanding, element replacement, quality verification, and result delivery. The service focuses on product and character consistency, detail restoration, conversion expression, and large-scale production. It supports targeted replacement of products or characters based on hit video templates. By retaining the original actions, camera rhythms, and marketing structures, it rapidly generates multi-version content to reduce shooting, editing, and adaptation costs.</para>
        /// <h2><b>Scenarios</b></h2>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><b>Video material variation:</b> Uses an existing e-commerce video as a template and replaces only specified products or characters in the video, preserving the original camera angles, rhythms, and marketing expressions as much as possible. This is suitable for producing materials with multiple SKUs, models, regions, and versions.</description></item>
        /// <item><description><b>Rapid material generation for new products:</b> For centrally launched new products, it reduces the need for live-action shooting, studio setup, post-production editing, and repetitive production. It rapidly deploys video materials for new products, helping merchants shorten the launch cycle from spotting hit videos to breaking down scripts and shooting new content.</description></item>
        /// <item><description><b>Product explanation and selling point expression:</b> Suitable for products such as apparel, beauty and personal care, food and beverages, home and daily necessities, 3C digital products, and small home appliances. It can plan the explanation structure, display actions, and camera rhythms based on the selling points of the original video, and generate explanation videos tailored for the conversion of new products.</description></item>
        /// <item><description><b>Multi-selling point and multi-version testing:</b> Rapidly generates multiple versions based on different product selling points, target audiences, scripts, camera angles, and visual styles. This supports merchants in conducting content testing and iterating on delivered materials.</description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <h2><b>Product capabilities</b></h2>
        /// <h3><b>Core capabilities</b></h3>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><para><b>Supports two replacement modes:</b></para>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><para><b>Product replacement (</b><c>product_replacement</c><b>)</b>: Retains the original video\&quot;s host identity, actions, scene, and sales structure, and replaces the original product with the target product.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Character replacement (</b><c>person_replacement</c><b>)</b>: Retains the original video\&quot;s product, actions, scene, and sales structure, and replaces the on-screen character with the target character from reference images or descriptions.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Supports two generation modes:</b></para>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><para><b>Reference generation (</b><c>reference</c><b>)</b>: 1:1 replication. Uses the original video as a complete reference to automatically generate a new video with the same duration as the original video. It retains the original script, storyboard, actions, scene, and rhythm, and only performs targeted replacement of specified content such as characters or products.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Rebuild generation (</b><c>rebuild</c><b>)</b>: Breaks down the script, storyboard, and key elements of the original video, retains only core content such as specified characters or products, and then redesigns and generates a new video. It is not limited by the original video duration and supports inputting a target duration.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Fully automated end-to-end generation with zero prompt threshold</b>: Only requires passing in the reference video and target product or character images. The system automatically completes the entire process of video understanding, script planning, storyboard design, first-frame generation, and video synthesis.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Product understanding and information structuring</b>: Identifies product categories, appearance, materials, colors, structures, and key components, and combines them with the titles, attributes, and selling points provided by merchants to generate usable video expression information.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Template video element replacement</b>: Supports replacing products or characters within the authorized scope, and defines the replacement scope and protection scope to reduce changes in non-target areas.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Product subject consistency</b>: Maintains the stability of the product\&quot;s shape, color, texture, pattern, packaging, and logo as much as possible across different camera angles, perspectives, actions, and scenes.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Product fidelity</b>: Multi-round VL quality inspection locks the product state (color, texture, structure, print) throughout the process to prevent product feature drift.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Selling point script and storyboard replication</b>: Follows the selling point planning, video structure, camera sequence, display actions, voiceover content, and ending style of the original video.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Commercial model adaptation</b>: Supports matching corresponding model images and display methods based on product style, fit, target audience, and market demand.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Quality verification and result feedback</b>: Conducts multi-dimensional checks on the product subject, characters, clothing, text, picture integrity, audio, and overall usability, and outputs result information for manual review.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// </description>
        /// 
        /// <param name="tmpReq">
        /// EcomVideoRecreationRequest
        /// </param>
        /// <param name="runtime">
        /// runtime options for this request RuntimeOptions
        /// </param>
        /// 
        /// <returns>
        /// EcomVideoRecreationResponse
        /// </returns>
