        /// <term><b>Summary:</b></term>
        /// <summary>
        /// <para>Removes unwanted elements from e-commerce images by automatically identifying and erasing text, specific names, transparent text blocks, watermarks, and clutter, and allows you to specify objects to be removed on demand. This synchronous operation efficiently and accurately processes large batches of images to simplify image editing.</para>
        /// </summary>
        /// 
        /// <term><b>Description:</b></term>
        /// <description>
        /// <h1>Product Introduction</h1>
        /// <para>The intelligent image object removal product is tailored for e-commerce images. It automatically identifies and removes text, specific names, transparent text blocks, and promotional stickers. You can specify objects to remove for efficient and accurate batch processing to simplify image editing. (Synchronous)</para>
        /// <h1>Scenarios</h1>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><b>Efficient e-commerce image processing:</b></description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <para>Removes irrelevant visual elements to provide clearer and more focused product displays, enhancing the customer shopping experience.</para>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><b>Multi-platform product information synchronization:</b></description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <para>When listing products on different e-commerce platforms, merchants can quickly remove specific text and promotional stickers to comply with the image specifications of different platforms.</para>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><b>Marketing material preparation:</b></description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <para>Merchants can easily remove original promotional information and quickly update it with the latest campaign information.</para>
        /// <remarks>
        /// <para>Note: Merchants or platforms can batch remove visual clutter from images to optimize image quality. Use this feature in combination with the Intelligent Recognition API (coming soon) to first filter images containing text, specific names, transparent text blocks, and promotional stickers, and then use the Intelligent Object Removal API for batch removal. The Intelligent Recognition API focuses on recognition, while the Intelligent Object Removal API focuses on removal. Calling them in sequence maximizes the removal effect and reduces false removals and false recognitions.</para>
        /// </remarks>
        /// <h1>Features</h1>
        /// <ol>
        /// <item><description><para>First, clarify the definitions of the image subject and the image background. When specifying the objects to remove, choose the image subject or the image background area as the removal scope. Both API and editor integration methods are supported to meet different types of requirements.</para>
        /// <ol>
        /// <item><description><para>Image subject: the core product area in the image.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para>Image background: the rest of the image excluding the product subject.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// </ol>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para>Second, the following three scenarios are supported for object removal:</para>
        /// <ol>
        /// <item><description><para>The user only selects the type. Text, specific names, transparent text blocks, and promotional stickers are supported. Refer to the following examples to clarify your requirements and perform targeted operations.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para>(Upgraded) Supports specifying image elements for removal. You can specify multiple image URLs at a time.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para>(Upgraded) Supports specifying text for removal. You can specify multiple text strings at a time.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// </ol>
