        /// <term><b>Summary:</b></term>
        /// <summary>
        /// <para>Detects the compliance of store marketing materials based on a multimodal large language model (MLLM) for offline retail and channel store inspection scenarios. Evaluates standard materials such as functional table cards, posters, and door display stands, as well as long-tail materials like light box cloths, KT boards, floor stickers, and light boxes in actual store photos against inspection rules at the natural language level, and outputs structured conclusions and Chinese evidence descriptions that can be directly integrated with business systems. This is a <b>synchronous</b> API operation that returns results in a single request.</para>
        /// </summary>
        /// 
        /// <term><b>Description:</b></term>
        /// <description>
        /// <h2><b>Scenarios</b></h2>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><para><b>Store marketing material compliance inspection</b>: Automatically determines whether specified marketing materials (feature table cards, posters, door display stands, etc.) are placed or posted in the store according to the standard display guidelines issued by the headquarters, and identifies typical issues such as &quot;not placed, placement fault, or content mismatch&quot;.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>New product or campaign material landing verification</b>: During new product publish or sales promotions, automatically verifies in batches whether campaign materials in actual store photos have completed listing as required, to override manual sampling inspections.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Adaptive dual-image comparison and single-image detection</b>: The same API operation supports both dual-image comparison (&quot;reference image + target image&quot;, Pattern A) and single-image detection (&quot;target image only&quot;, Pattern B). It performs automatic switchover based on whether <c>ImageRefer</c> is passed, so invokers do not need to distinguish between invoke methods.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <h2><b>Features</b></h2>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><para><b>Multi-mode intelligent routing</b>: Built-in material type parsing capability. Automatically identifies the target material type based on the natural language text in <c>Rules</c> and routes it to the corresponding material detection pipeline. Callers only need to pass the image URL and rule text. Currently, four detection item routes are supported: &quot;functional table card&quot;, &quot;poster&quot;, &quot;door display stand&quot;, and &quot;other materials&quot;. Detection pipelines for more specific marketing material types will be added in the future.</para>
        /// </description></item>
