        /// <term><b>Summary:</b></term>
        /// <summary>
        /// <para>Detects product displays in physical stores by using a multimodal large language model (MLLM) and visual vector recall. This capability is designed for shelf and floor display inspection scenarios in offline retail and channel stores. The API processes real-world shelf and floor display images captured in stores, uses the MLLM to detect the border box and preliminary name of each product, and then performs similarity recall against a customer-specific SKU vector database to perform an exact match of each product to the customer\&quot;s own SKUs. It outputs structured, per-product results that can be directly integrated with business systems. This API is suitable for large-scale, high-concurrency visual recognition pipelines, such as remote auditing of offline store displays by headquarters, SKU distribution verification, and display compliance inspections.</para>
        /// </summary>
        /// 
        /// <term><b>Description:</b></term>
        /// <description>
        /// <h2><b>Product Introduction</b></h2>
        /// <para>Product display detection is an intelligent recognition capability built on a multimodal large language model (MLLM) and visual vector recall, designed for shelf and floor display inspection scenarios in offline retail and channel stores. The service processes real-world shelf and floor display images captured in stores, uses the MLLM to detect the border box and preliminary name of each product, and then performs similarity recall against a customer-specific SKU vector database to perform an exact match of each product to the customer\&quot;s own SKUs. It outputs structured, per-product results that can be directly integrated with business systems. This service is suitable for large-scale, high-concurrency visual recognition pipelines, such as remote auditing of offline store displays by headquarters, SKU distribution verification, and display compliance inspections.</para>
        /// <h2><b>Scenarios</b></h2>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><para><b>Shelf and floor display recognition and inventory</b>: Recognizes each product in a shelf or floor display image and matches it to the customer\&quot;s SKU database, outputting a per-product list (product name + location + similarity score) to replace manual counting.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Distribution verification and SKU compliance</b>: Verifies whether stores display specified SKUs as required by headquarters and checks for out-of-stock or misplaced items, supporting batch automatic verification during sales promotions or new product launches.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Customer-specific SKU database</b>: Customers can upload their own standard SKU images to create a dedicated vector database (isolated by <c>RagId</c>). During recognition, retrieval is performed only within the customer\&quot;s database to ensure accurate naming and data isolation between customers.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <h2><b>Features</b></h2>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><para><b>Two-stage collaboration of detection and retrieval</b>: The MLLM detects the bounding box and preliminary name of each product in the entire image (semantic-level understanding, adapted to dense displays and partial occlusion). Then, visual embedding vectors are used to perform similarity retrieval within the customer\&quot;s SKU database, and the top-1 exact SKU name overwrites the preliminary name, balancing the recall rate and naming accuracy.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Isolated retrieval in dedicated vector databases</b>: A dedicated SKU vector database is maintained for each customer based on <c>RagId</c>. Recognition retrieves data only within the corresponding database, ensuring strict isolation between customers. Added or updated SKUs take effect in real time.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Structured per-product output</b>: Structured output is unified as <c>Result.Items[]</c>. Each product independently provides the bounding box, retrieved SKU name, SKU code, and similarity score, which can directly drive downstream inventory and verification systems and support case-level manual review and tracing.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Supported input formats</b>: Currently supports image URLs accessible over the Internet or from OSS. A single shelf or floor display image can be recognized, and structured output structure is unified.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// </description>
        /// 
