        /// <term><b>Summary:</b></term>
        /// <summary>
        /// <para>Translates the speech and on-screen text in a video into a target language. You can select speech subtitle translation, on-screen text translation, or both. This API applies to scenarios such as multilingual distribution of e-commerce videos, international social media marketing, and global brand advertising. The API uses an asynchronous invocation mode. After you submit a translation task, you can obtain the task ID and poll the task status by calling the query API until the task is completed and the result is returned.</para>
        /// </summary>
        /// 
        /// <term><b>Description:</b></term>
        /// <description>
        /// <h2>Product introduction</h2>
        /// <para>The video translation API translates the speech and on-screen text in a video into a target language. You can select speech subtitle translation, on-screen text translation, or both. This API applies to scenarios such as multilingual distribution of e-commerce videos, international social media marketing, and global brand advertising.
        /// The API uses an asynchronous invocation mode. After you submit a translation task, you can obtain the <c>TaskId</c> and poll the task status by calling the query API until the task is completed and the result is returned.</para>
        /// <h2>Scenarios</h2>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><para><b>Cross-border e-commerce video localization</b>: Translates the speech subtitles and selling point text in product introduction videos into the language of the target market to facilitate promotion on overseas platforms.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>International social media marketing</b>: Localizes speech subtitles and on-screen text for platforms such as TikTok, Instagram, and YouTube with a single click to improve comprehension and conversion rates among overseas users.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Global brand advertising</b>: Automatically generates video versions in the languages of the target regions to reduce manual production costs.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><para><b>Training and product instructions</b>: Translates the speech subtitles and on-screen text in training courses or product demo videos into multiple languages for global teams.</para>
        /// </description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <h2>Features</h2>
        /// <table>
        /// <thead>
        /// <tr>
        /// <th>Feature</th>
        /// <th>Identifier</th>
        /// <th>Description</th>
        /// </tr>
        /// </thead>
        /// <tbody><tr>
        /// <td>Speech subtitle translation</td>
        /// <td><c>speech</c></td>
        /// <td>Translates the video speech into target language dubbing. You can choose to only erase the original subtitles or replace them with translated subtitles. By default, the original subtitles are not processed and no new subtitles are added.</td>
        /// </tr>
        /// <tr>
        /// <td>On-screen text translation</td>
        /// <td><c>visual</c></td>
        /// <td>Translates the source language text in the video frames, or only erases the on-screen text without translation. You can choose to erase brand logos.</td>
        /// </tr>
        /// <tr>
        /// <td>Speech subtitle translation (<c>speech</c>) generates target language dubbing based on the spoken content in the video, processes the subtitles according to the original subtitle processing option, and synthesizes the final video. Original subtitles refer to the existing subtitles in the video frames that correspond to the spoken content. Replacing with translated subtitles first erases the original subtitles and then adds subtitles synchronized with the translated speech.</td>
        /// <td></td>
        /// <td></td>
        /// </tr>
        /// <tr>
        /// <td>On-screen text translation (<c>visual</c>) targets recognizable original video language text in the video frames, such as titles, product selling points, and descriptive text. It can be used independently without selecting speech subtitle translation first, and does not require the text to appear in the speech. Original subtitles within the processing scope may also be processed.</td>
        /// <td></td>
        /// <td></td>
        /// </tr>
        /// <tr>
        /// <td>When both <c>speech</c> and <c>visual</c> are selected, the speech subtitle translation is completed and the video is synthesized first. Then, on-screen text processing is performed on this video, retaining the translated dubbing, and a final video is output. The order of features in the array does not affect the execution order. Therefore, not processing original subtitles only means that no subtitles are erased or added during the speech subtitle phase, and subsequent on-screen text processing may still alter the original subtitles. Subtitles that have been replaced with translated ones will be retained during subsequent on-screen text processing.</td>
