        /// <h2>Scenarios</h2>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><b>Virtual try-on for apparel:</b>
        /// Supports various apparel categories such as tops, bottoms, jumpsuits, and dresses. After you upload a model image and a garment image, the service generates natural and realistic try-on effects to intuitively showcase how the garment looks on the model.</description></item>
        /// <item><description><b>Virtual try-on for shoes and hats:</b>
        /// Supports virtual try-on for shoes and hats. The service intelligently matches the position and proportion of the product based on the model\&quot;s pose and body parts to present a coordinated and realistic wearing effect.</description></item>
        /// <item><description><b>E-commerce product display and marketing:</b>
        /// Helps merchants quickly generate model try-on images for different products, reducing the costs of traditional photography, outfit changes, and post-production, and improving the production efficiency of product images.</description></item>
        /// <item><description><b>Online shopping experience optimization:</b>
        /// Allows consumers to preview the wearing effect of products through virtual try-on, providing a more intuitive understanding of the style, matching, and overall effect of the products to assist in purchase decisions and enhance the shopping experience.</description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <h2>Features</h2>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><b>First, you need to provide a model image and a product image. The system uses the model image as the try-on subject and applies the garment from the product image to the model:</b><list type="bullet">
