        /// <para>Generates virtual try-on images by replacing the clothing on a model with a specified garment based on AI algorithms. The service preserves the model\&quot;s details, pose, and facial features while ensuring a realistic and well-fitted appearance. You can obtain processed images by providing the URLs of the original model and garment images.</para>
        /// </summary>
        /// 
        /// <term><b>Description:</b></term>
        /// <description>
        /// <para><em>Note:</em>*
        /// VirtualTryOn is an early version that supports only single-garment try-on and is scheduled to be deprecated soon.
        /// The new capabilities for multi-garment matching, model replacement, and pose replacement are now available in <a href="https://api.aliyun.com/document/Aidge/2026-04-28/AiTryOn">Virtual try-on (AiTryOn)</a>. Please refer to the new API for integration.</para>
        /// <h2>Scenarios</h2>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><b>Virtual try-on for apparel:</b>
        /// Supports various apparel categories such as tops, bottoms, jumpsuits, and dresses. After you upload a model image and a garment image, the service generates natural and realistic try-on effects to intuitively showcase how the garment looks on the model.</description></item>
        /// <item><description><b>Virtual try-on for shoes and hats:</b>
        /// Supports virtual try-on for shoes and hats. The service intelligently matches the position and proportion of the product based on the model\&quot;s pose and body parts to present a coordinated and realistic wearing effect.</description></item>
        /// <item><description><b>E-commerce product display and marketing:</b>
        /// Helps merchants quickly generate model try-on images for different products, reducing the costs of traditional photography, outfit changes, and post-production, and improving the production efficiency of product images.</description></item>
        /// <item><description><b>Online shopping experience optimization:</b>
        /// Allows consumers to preview the wearing effect of products through virtual try-on, providing a more intuitive understanding of the style, matching, and overall effect of the products to assist in purchase decisions and enhance the shopping experience.</description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <h2>Features</h2>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><b>First, you need to provide a model image and a product image. The system uses the model image as the try-on subject and applies the garment from the product image to the model:</b><list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description>a. Model image: The image of the person for the virtual try-on.</description></item>
        /// <item><description>b. Product image: The image of the garment, shoes, or hat to be worn by the model.</description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><b>Second, you can select the corresponding product type based on the actual product. Supported types include tops, bottoms, jumpsuits, dresses, shoes, and hats:</b><list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description>a. Specify product type: You can directly specify the type of the current product, and the system will process it accordingly.</description></item>
        /// <item><description>b. Automatic type recognition: If you do not specify the product type, the system automatically recognizes the product category in the product image and performs the virtual try-on based on the recognition result.</description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// </description></item>
        /// <item><description><b>Finally, the system generates a virtual try-on image by combining the model image, product image, and product type to showcase the wearing effect of the product on the model:</b><list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description>a. Preserve model details: The generation process does not alter the appearance, hairstyle, pose, body shape, or other details of the person in the original model image.</description></item>
        /// <item><description>b. Maintain image consistency: The background, composition, lighting, and overall visual effect of the original model image remain unchanged. Only the wearing area corresponding to the product is processed.</description></item>
        /// <item><description>c. Generate try-on effect: The product is naturally applied to the model, fitting the person\&quot;s pose and body structure to generate a coordinated and realistic virtual try-on image.</description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// </description></item>
        /// </list>
